# ── open-cowork configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored). NEVER commit real keys.
#
# There are TWO independent ways to drive the agent. Pick either — or set both
# and switch in Settings.
#
#   A. COASTY  — the hosted computer-use API (cloud machines + a tuned CUA model)
#   B. BYO LLM — your own key from any provider, driving YOUR screen locally
#
# ── A. Coasty ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#    • Set COASTY_API_KEY  → the whole product talks to the real Coasty API.
#                            Use a sandbox key (sk-coasty-test-*) — it never bills.
#    • Leave it UNSET      → DEMO MODE: `pnpm dev` boots the bundled mock Coasty
#                            server and the backend uses an ephemeral sandbox key.
#                            Zero account, zero spend, full product end-to-end.

# Your Coasty API key (sandbox keys start with sk-coasty-test- and never bill).
# Create one at https://coasty.ai/developers/keys
COASTY_API_KEY=

# ── B. Bring your own model (local runs, `pnpm desktop`) ─────────────────────
#
# Set ONE of these and the desktop app picks it up automatically at startup —
# no clicking through Settings. The model is auto-selected (first vision-capable
# model the provider lists) unless you pin one with COWORK_LLM_MODEL.
#
# Computer use is screenshot-driven, so the model MUST accept images. A
# text-only model is refused up front rather than failing on the first step.

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter (one key, most models) — https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# If you set MORE THAN ONE of the keys above, open-cowork will refuse to guess
# and ask you to name one here. Values: anthropic | openai | google |
# openrouter | openai-compatible
# COWORK_LLM_PROVIDER=

# Pin an exact model instead of auto-selecting one.
#   COWORK_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#   COWORK_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o
# COWORK_LLM_MODEL=

# Local / self-hosted models (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM) and OpenAI-dialect
# gateways (Together, Groq, Fireworks). Point at the /v1 endpoint; most local
# servers need no key.
#   COWORK_LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
#   COWORK_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   COWORK_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-vl
# COWORK_LLM_BASE_URL=
# COWORK_LLM_API_KEY=

# ── Optional overrides (sensible defaults; you can delete all of these) ───────

# Coasty API base. Auto-resolves: the bundled mock in demo mode, else the real
# API. Override to pin one explicitly.
#   real:  https://coasty.ai/v1
#   mock:  http://127.0.0.1:4010/v1
# COASTY_BASE_URL=

# Backend bind + port.
# COWORK_PORT=4000
# COWORK_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Public URL Coasty uses to deliver webhooks back to this backend (https in prod).
# COWORK_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# SQLite path (':memory:' for ephemeral).
# COWORK_DB_PATH=./data/cowork.sqlite

# Secret backing client session tokens. Auto-generated if unset (tokens then do
# not survive a restart). Set a stable 32+ char value in production.
# COWORK_SESSION_SECRET=

# Server-enforced default per-run spending cap, in USD cents.
# COWORK_DEFAULT_BUDGET_CENTS=500

# Force the mock even with a key set (handy for offline demos).
# COWORK_USE_MOCK=1

# Opt-in live sandbox smoke tests (sk-coasty-test-* + COASTY_BASE_URL=real only).
# COWORK_RUN_LIVE=
